    "narrative": "With the league calendar reaching October 17th, the Austin Waves face a constrained slate where our primary offensive producers like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined by off-days. Consequently, we are leaning heavily on **Liam Hicks** (55.93), our strongest start today. **Liam Hicks** holds a marginal-plus rating, benefiting from an advantageous platoon split against the right-handed Shawn Armstrong (4.35 xERA). While we are awaiting official confirmation, the expectation that **Liam Hicks** slots into the cleanup spot provides a meaningful lift to his RBI floor, making him our most reliable asset for today\u2019s limited utility.\n\nThe rest of the lineup requires surgical discipline to navigate. **Brayan Rocchio** (49.70) remains in the lineup as a utility filler, though his value is suppressed by his assumed position at the bottom of the order. The delta between **Brayan Rocchio** and our other bench options was negligible, but he remains active largely due to the moderate SP matchup against Nick Martinez; we are counting on volume over ceiling here. It is a quiet day for the roster, with **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL and the remainder of our deep bench\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014all inactive due to scheduling. We are playing for efficiency rather than explosion, keeping a tight watch on any late-breaking lineup changes that might adjust the situational projections for **Liam Hicks** or **Brayan Rocchio**.",
